---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>About</p>
    <h1 data-reveal style="--d:80ms">Data, from both <span class="hl">sides of the table.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead" data-reveal style="--d:160ms">
      I'm {SITE.name}, a data and business intelligence analyst based in {SITE.location}.
    </p>

    <p>
      Since {SITE.since} I have worked across data analysis, business intelligence, ERP systems
      and product management in IT startups, telecom and fintech. My work has included building
      dashboards, implementing SAP Business One and training the people who use these systems
      every day.
    </p>
    <p>
      That mix means I look at data from both sides: the technical side of getting it out of
      systems and into shape, and the business side of making sure the numbers answer real
      questions and that people know how to use them.
    </p>

    <h2 data-reveal>What I'm learning now</h2>
    <p>
      I am building skills in analytics engineering — SQL data modelling, dbt, data testing and
      automated pipelines. Rather than just collecting certificates, I am building real
      projects on realistic business problems and publishing them on the
      <a href="/projects/">projects page</a>, including what worked and what didn't.
    </p>

    <h2 data-reveal>How I work</h2>
    <ul class="principles" data-reveal>
      <li>Start with the business question, not the tool.</li>
      <li>Keep solutions simple enough for your team to maintain.</li>
      <li>Document the logic so numbers can be checked and trusted.</li>
      <li>Be honest about what the data can and cannot tell you.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .principles { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .principles li {
    margin: 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0; background: var(--surface);
  }
</style>
